WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.673
Did you know that

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.808
people are voluntarily

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.310
putting tapeworms

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.579
inside their bodies?

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.415
It's known as the tapeworm diet.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.983
It helps people lose weight

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.818
by letting this parasite 

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.719
eat everything

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.287
inside of them.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.922
But this diet can go

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:26.526
very, very wrong.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.065
Well on today's challenge

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.199
we're going to find out

00:00:33.199 --> 00:00:34.534
by having you

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.569
swallow a tapeworm.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:38.772
Think you can handle it?

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.578
Tapeworms are flat,

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.846
segmented worms

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.615
that can be as long as

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.117
25 meters (80 feet).

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.519
They can’t live

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.820
freely on their own,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.121
they need to be

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:55.955
in the gut

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:56.756
of an animal

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.992
or a human to thrive.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.560
Animals can become infected

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.828
with these parasites

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.596
when grazing in pastures

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.133
or drinking contaminated water.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.234
How long do you think

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.235
a tapeworm

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.804
can live inside your body?

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:16.709
We'll have your answer

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.511
later in the episode.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.516
There are two ways to get infected.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.517
The most common

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.819
tapeworm infection

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.321
is called

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.089
You get this 

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:29.989
if you eat

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.158
undercooked meat or fish

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.860
from an infected animal.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.395
The tapeworm larvae

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.230
in the animal muscle tissue

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.166
would migrate to your gut.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.701
You can also get infected

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.236
if you are in contact with 

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.304
animal faeces 

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.306
or contaminated water

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.975
from an animal with tapeworms.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.310
This type of infection

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.979
is known as

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:53.980
You get this

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.081
by ingesting

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.750
microscopic tapeworm eggs.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.019
It’s rare to get a parasite this way.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.654
But it can happen

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.889
in countries

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.792
with poor sanitary conditions.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.727
In both scenarios,

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.363
you wouldn’t feel a thing.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:14.734
If you have a cysticercosis infection,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.569
the eggs you ingested

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.072
will hatch into mobile larvae

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.674
once they've entered your intestines. 

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.209
They could migrate

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.878
out of your intestines

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:26.613
and infect organs

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.915
other than the digestive system. 

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.417
But throughout your first week,

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.752
it's likely you won't notice

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.420
anything at all.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.255
So let's see what happens

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.990
when we keep going.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.059
Let’s go back to the

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.829
taeniasis infection.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.164
The tapeworm larva 

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.331
has developed into

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.699
an adult tapeworm.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.901
in your intestines

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.770
and can be up to 7 m (23 ft) long.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.639
It attaches to the inner wall

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:53.940
of your intestines

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.642
and feeds off the food

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.477
you’re digesting.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:02:59.546
You could feel nauseous,

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:01.347
have abdominal pain,

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:02.448
diarrhea,

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.418
and you'd begin to lose weight.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:08.021
But it's also very likely that

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.356
you wouldn't feel anything at all.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:11.124
You may find out

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.292
you have tapeworms

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.561
by taking a closer look at

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.329
what you've produced

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.464
while on the toilet seat.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.599
At this stage,

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.201
pieces of the tapeworm

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.268
break off and

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.503
exit your body 

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:25.171
via your stool.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:28.408
And they look just like tiny worms.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.910
Gross.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.879
Now that you've finally found out

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.581
you have tapeworms.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:37.350
It's time to go to the doctor.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.886
If you’re diagnosed with taeniasis,

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.821
your doctor will prescribe

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:44.624
oral medication for one day.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.925
It would paralyze

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.694
the adult tapeworm,

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:50.163
which would let go of the intestine,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.864
dissolve, and

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.734
exit your body via your stool.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.636
If the worms are large,

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.470
you could have

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.871
some stomach cramping

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:01.107
when they pass.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.178
Ok, you managed to escape

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.647
a taeniasis infection but

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:08.715
what if you had

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:11.184
cysticercosis instead?

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.152
Well, if three months have passed

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.520
and you haven't noticed

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.022
this infection,

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.824
things would get terrible.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.292
A stomach cramp or

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.127
sudden weight loss would be

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.696
the last thing you're worried about.

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.665
That's because the mobile larvae

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.866
that have migrated

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.735
throughout your entire body

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:31.304
are mature enough to form cysts

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.373
in tissues like your lungs,

00:04:33.373 --> 00:04:36.576
brain, eyes, or liver.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.744
These cysts could

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.078
grow large enough

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:40.813
to crowd the functioning parts

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.015
of the organ or

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.183
reduce its blood supply.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.718
You could have headaches or

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.520
or allergic reactions.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.255
You might experience seizures

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.791
in extreme cases.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.259
To get rid of these worms,

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.961
you would need surgery

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.797
or an organ transplant.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.201
And even after 20 years,

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:03.936
it's still possible

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.271
that the tapeworm

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:07.407
could live inside of you,

00:05:07.407 --> 00:05:09.609
without you even knowing.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.678
And your buddy could measure

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.947
more than 25 m (80 ft) long.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.282
And if the tapeworm

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.384
continued to grow,

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.286
you would eventually experience

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:21.554
a digestive problem

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.423
as it blocks your appendix

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:26.492
or pancreatic ducts.

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:29.295
So tapeworms are horrible

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:30.963
and creepy, and

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.131
you don't want them

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.666
anywhere near you,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:37.236
regardless of the easy weight loss.

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.105
Speaking of weight loss,

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.840
how about the opposite?

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.343
Like gaining 300 lb (136 kg)

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.678
in a single year?

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:46.279
Well,

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:48.348
we'll see what that challenge brings

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.283
on another episode of

